      "extract": "[]{#sec:octahedral-colorings label=\"sec:octahedral-colorings\"} ::: definition The of a tangle $T$ is its complement as a submanifold of $[0,1]^{3}$. We write $\\pi(T)$ for the fundamental group of the complement. Suppose $T$ has $n$ incoming and $m$ outgoing boundary points and let $D$ be a diagram of $T$. We can think of $D$ as a decorated $4$-valent graph $G$ embedded in $[0,1] \\times [0,1]$ with $n$ edges",
